{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-10-Nov-2022-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "If the number 476 ** 0 is divisible by both 3 and 11, then in the hundredth and tenth places, the non-zero digits are, respectively:", "options": [{"text": "2 and 3", "added": false}, {"text": "3 and 2", "added": false}, {"text": "5 and 8", "added": false}, {"text": "8 and 5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "The height and curved surface area of a right circular cylinder are 7 cm and 70 π cm2. Its total surface area is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "A cylinder of height 8 cm and radius 6 cm is melted and converted into 3 cones of the same radius and height that of cylinder. Determine the total curved surface area of cones.", "options": [{"text": "180 π cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "60 π cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "144 π cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "120 π cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "The heights of two right circular cones are in the ratio 1 : 5 and the perimeter of their bases are in the ratio 5 : 3. Find the ratio of their volumes.", "options": [{"text": "8 : 11", "added": false}, {"text": "7 : 6", "added": false}, {"text": "5 : 9", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Two trains 121m and 99m in length, respectively, are running in opposite directions, one at a speed of 40 km/h and the other at a speed of 32 km/h. In what time will they be completely clear of each other from the moment they meet?", "options": [{"text": "11 sec", "added": false}, {"text": "12 sec", "added": false}, {"text": "13 sec", "added": false}, {"text": "10 sec", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "The cost price of an article is ₹1,200. On buying four such articles, the customer gets one for free. If the selling price of each article is ₹1,800, then determine the net percentage profit earned by the shop keeper on selling four articles.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "articles-and-batches", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "Find the difference between the compound interest and simple interest when a sum of Rs.15,625 is invested for 3 years at 4% per annum.", "options": [{"text": "Rs.76", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.96", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.56", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.86", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "si-ci-difference", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "Barley", "added": false}, {"text": "Others", "added": false}, {"text": "Wheat", "added": false}, {"text": "Rice", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "33.4", "added": false}, {"text": "32.6", "added": false}, {"text": "35.8", "added": false}, {"text": "34.2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "How much percentage should a racer increase speed to reduce the time by 20% to cover a fixed distance?", "options": [{"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "40%", "added": false}, {"text": "35%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "If 86y5 is exactly divisible by 3, then the least value of y is:", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Simplify the following: (1 + cot2θ)(1 − cos θ)(1 + cos θ)", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "-5", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "-3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "Two circles of radii 8 cm and 3 cm, respectively, are 13 cm apart. AB is a direct common tangent touch to both the circles at A and B respectively then the length of AB is", "options": [{"text": "10 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "12 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "8 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "6 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "If the radius of a sphere increases by 10%, what would be the change in the surface area of the sphere?", "options": [{"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "21%", "added": false}, {"text": "31%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "April, June", "added": false}, {"text": "April, July", "added": false}, {"text": "July, September", "added": false}, {"text": "April, May", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "29°", "added": false}, {"text": "38°", "added": false}, {"text": "54°", "added": false}, {"text": "68°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "A and B run a 12 km race on a circular track of length 1200 m. They complete one round in 300 seconds and 400 seconds, respectively. After how much time from start will the faster person meet the slower person for the last time?", "options": [{"text": "2400 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "8400 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "9600 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "10800 seconds", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "circular-track", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "The perimeters of two similar triangles are 36 cm and 24 cm, respectively. Find the ratio of their areas.", "options": [{"text": "6 : 13", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "9 : 4", "added": false}, {"text": "35 : 24", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "Satish bought 35 notebooks for ₹700 and sold 28 of them for ₹600. Find his percentage gain.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "remainder-based", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "The ratio of two numbers is 5 : 7 and their HCF is 3. Their LCM is:", "options": [{"text": "75", "added": false}, {"text": "105", "added": false}, {"text": "125", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "A shopkeeper gives 20% commission on the retail price of one article and earns 5% profit. If his commission is reduced by 10%, then what is his approximate profit percentage? (Nearest integral value)", "options": [{"text": "18%", "added": false}, {"text": "10%", "added": false}, {"text": "15%", "added": false}, {"text": "8%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "If cosθ + secθ = 2, then the value of sin6 θ + cos6 θ is: ⁡", "options": [{"text": "1/3", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "1/2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "The average of a batsman in 16 innings is 36. In the next innings, he scores 70 runs. What will be his new average?", "options": [{"text": "53", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}, {"text": "106", "added": false}, {"text": "38", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "The salary of Ramesh first increases by 35%, then decreases by 40%, then again increases by 25%. Find the overall increase or decrease percentage.", "options": [{"text": "Increase 1.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "Decrease 2.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "Decrease 1.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increase 2.25%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "The average age of 25 girls in a class is 11.2 years and that of the remaining 15 girls is 10 years. Find the average age of all the girls in the class.", "options": [{"text": "10.75 years", "added": false}, {"text": "11.35 years", "added": false}, {"text": "10.45 years", "added": false}, {"text": "11.05 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "average-age", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "More by 31.2 Percent", "added": false}, {"text": "Less by 31.2 Percent", "added": false}, {"text": "Less by 38.9 Percent", "added": false}, {"text": "More by 38.9 Percent", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "A retailer wants to sell an item for Rs.2,700 after granting a 10% discount. What is the marked price of the item?", "options": [{"text": "Rs.2,850", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.3,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.3,050", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.3,110", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-fractions", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "125", "added": false}, {"text": "112", "added": false}, {"text": "130", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "12%", "added": false}, {"text": "13%", "added": false}, {"text": "11.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "12.5%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "Find the least value of (A + B) if the number 27B58A4 is completely divisible by 88.", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "A can complete a work in 8 days and B can complete the same work in 11 days. How long will they take, if both work together?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "A bus travels at 100km/h for the first 1/2 hour. Later it travels at 80km/h. Find the time taken by the bus to travel 290 km.", "options": [{"text": "4 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "3.5 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "3 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "2.5 hours", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "early-late", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "The value of (cosec A + cot A)(1 - cos A) is:", "options": [{"text": "cos A", "added": false}, {"text": "tan A", "added": false}, {"text": "cot A", "added": false}, {"text": "sin A", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "A and B can complete a work in 36 days and 45 days respectively. They worked together for 2 days and then A left the work. In how many days will B complete the remaining work?", "options": [{"text": "41.5", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "41", "added": false}, {"text": "40.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "52", "added": false}, {"text": "64", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3 : 1",